WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.310
Welcome to the Transhuman Daily, Friday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.990
Here are the last 24 hours in transhumanism, in 3 minutes.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:15.630
Level up.

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.880
Outside reviewers say Anthropic's AI is now improving about twice as fast.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:26.750
Roughly two years of progress in one, mostly because AI now helps build AI.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.760
Meanwhile, OpenAI says its cyber AI found 81 serious,

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.130
unknown Firefox flaws; Mozilla's fixing them.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:43.800
In Sydney, flipping one tiny bit sent an AI's training somewhere else,

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:45.190
nearly half the time.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:49.110
And in gerbils, hearing implants that use light,

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:52.140
not electricity, sent clearer, more distinct signals.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.790
Plus, a USC AI fills the torn corners of brain-wiring scans,

00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:59.530
to track ageing brains.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:00.860
In longevity,

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:07.340
a blood-pressure drug plus vibration seemed to flush Alzheimer's proteins from 29 healthy brains.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.480
And women with more years of natural estrogen show

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:13.450
ed fewer signs of brain blood-vessel damage at 70.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.060
Pandemic stress sped up epigenetic ageing clocks,

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:21.480
and for teens, how stressed they felt really mattered.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.520
Closer to home,

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:29.920
older Queenslanders' heart rates rose almost twice as fast per degree once homes passed 26°C.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.430
For wellbeing, in over 300,000 Brits,

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:36.360
loneliness went with being biologically a few months older.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.490
And in Melbourne,

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:43.950
one dose of psilocybin eased a schizophrenia-like filtering problem in female mice, for days.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.050
Now, the catch.

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:52.430
Novartis says nine tumours were reported among over 6,000 kids given its SMA gene therapy.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.860
And a month of online loving-kindness meditation e

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:59.230
ased pain no better than simple muscle relaxation.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.050
On the frontier, a robot moth grew itself a new light sensor,

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:07.970
using its artificial blood.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:11.270
A preprint reckons 23,000 cat qubits could cr

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:14.170
ack bank-grade encryption in about three days.

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:18.730
And Harvard's Wyss Institute used DNA switches t

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:21.990
o sift 400 million molecules for new drug leads.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:23.010
Level up,

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:27.370
together: smarter tools matter most when they buy all of us more good years.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.550
Every day, the curve gets a little steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.710
Somehow, the future keeps landing early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.350
That's one day of news. Imagine what a year looks like.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.340
That's the Transhuman Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.330
Stay well. Same time tomorrow?

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.600
Want more? Meet us in North Sydney on November 27.
